a boat trip on the zemptenberg lake is a  great way to start a tour of the laozits  lake region  the lake offers a range of recreational  activities  and many natural attractions around  forty thousand people vacation here  every year the ultimate plan is to  transform the entire former coal mining  complex into a tourist region  we're turning from miners into boat  captains by that i mean these mines are  becoming the blue eyes of the laozits  if you fly over a helicopter or plane  you see this wonderful blue landscape  the laozits lake region lies between the  states of brandenburg and saxony  the lakes were formed by filling with  water nine open cast mines that have  been closed down  by 2021 there will be 23 lakes all  together  anyone who wants to get a more elevated  look across the landscape  should head for the rusty nail it's a 30  meter high viewing tower that offers  visitors a unique look over  the water including zaidlitz lake  just a stone's throw away the geiservald  lake  here you can indulge in more physical  activities  or if you like just relax  if you want more you can rent a floating  apartment depending on the season  accommodations like these range from  between about 100 to almost  300 euros a night and people who have  their own boat can dock right in front  of their own door  people can relax here the apartments are  very well equipped  the unique thing is that this place  where we are right now was once an open  pit mine  this is where the coal was  around 2 billion tons of lignite were  mined and allows its region starting in  the middle of the 19th century onwards  and lignite is still mined here today  like in belzo  one major energy supplier offers  excursions  into the open kit mine's  this tour offers you an authentic mining  experience  you can see all the machinery such as  the rotary excavators  and the conveyor bridge in the  background it's moving the sand from one  side to the other  and there's real coal here you can pick  it up and feel it  after the lignite has been mined the  shafts that remain are up to 100 meters  deep  these are then flooded with water from  the nearby rivers  but it takes up to 20 years to form a  lake  if you want to get around the region a  bit faster you can explore on quads  incline pot bits you can take a quad  tour for between  60 and 200 euros  absolutely super great it's better than  driving a car  easier than riding a bike and you can't  top that  that was a blast tour includes a stop at  a lake that hasn't been completed yet  the part of its lake is due to open in  2014  by then the landscape will have had a  chance to adapt  one big attraction is the new sluice  gate on the koshner canal  the lock is the gateway between the  different water levels of the  geyservault  and zamtenberg lakes  makes sure that boats pass easily from  one lake to the other  side the lock has been open since the  first of june this year and we've  already had two thousand boats pass  through  that's a sign that the sluice gate is  very popular  by 2018 10 lakes here in the laozits  region will be connected by canals and  locks  and back to the new harbor on  zemptenberg lake  as a beautiful summer's day draws to a  close  it's beautiful here and the cycle routes  mean you can get everywhere on a bike  we want to see more and do more here the  countryside here is wonderful  and it's quiet  where a former industrial center has  become a recreation destination  where machinery once roared tourists can  now enjoy  peace and quiet  which european destination would you  like to see the most  which city which landmarks and which  scenery we'll be making your dreams come  true in our new regular slot  euromax extra tour let us know what  you'd like to see in the program  we'll select one of your suggestions go  on an extra tour for you  and name you on the program extra tour  our new weekly slot on euromax  here's how to get in touch write to us  at dw euromax voltastrossa 6  13355 berlin germany send us a fax to 49  for germany 3-0 for berlin  4646-6505  email us at euromax dot english dw dot  de
 

